<title>UK: MIDLAND RAISES UK BASE RATE TO 7.00 PCT.</title>
<headline>MIDLAND RAISES UK BASE RATE TO 7.00 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Midland Bank, part of HSBC Group, said on Thursday it raised its UK base interest rate to 7.00 percent from 6.75 percent, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The move followed a similar move by the Bank of England in its money market dealing rates.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
